[en.C08_DESC]
In the chaos of the Ultimate Battle in 999, Starlight Glimmer was lucky enough to escape. Exhausted, unconscious and lost most of her magic, Starlight Glimmer was sent to the Central Hospital of Ponyville for treatment, and managed to escape from the hospital before the pursuers of the “Big Three” arrived. At that time, Ponyville was in the middle of an agricultural reform, and the security forces of Ponyville were organizing to cut down the apple trees in Sweet Apple Acres. On the one hand, the cut wood would be used as fuel reserves, and on the other hand, more cold-resistant crops would be planted. Starlight Glimmer escaped to Sweet Apple Acres, took advantage of the chaos to steal some wood as a poor substitute for the train fuel, and hijacked a train that stopped in Ponyville, fleeing Ponyville with other fugitives. Although the train encountered an “accident” that was suspected to be planned by Cozy Glow on the way, Starlight was still lucky enough to survive, and arrived in Our Town in the autumn of 1000.\n\nIn the winter of 1001, she finally got in contact with Discord, who had escaped from the Ultimate Battle with her. He was now hiding in the Everfree Forest and fighting a guerrilla war against the Empire. Starlight and Discord quickly established the United Resistance, intending to attack the Empire when Cozy Glow was not yet stable in power. But it was already too late. The winter of 1001 is already two years after the Ultimate Battle, and Cozy Glow has gradually stabilized the situation, and the counterattack was swift. The United Resistance was able to advance for a small distance towards the Empire, but soon began to retreat. Before the front line of Starlight and Discord was cut off by the Empire, Discord gave Starlight a precious item that was found in the ruins of Twilight’s Castle — a diary. Starlight knew that it was the diary that connected the two worlds.\n\nIt is now the winter of 1002. The resistance army is still alive, inheriting the will of Celestia and Twilight, preserving the fire of harmonism. It has become a haven, a beacon of Equestria, illuminating the hope of all ponies.

[en.PIHC_WS_C08_desc]
In the chaos of the Ultimate Battle in 999, Starlight Glimmer was lucky enough to escape. Exhausted, unconscious and lost most of her magic, Starlight Glimmer was sent to the Central Hospital of Ponyville for treatment, and managed to escape from the hospital before the pursuers of the “Big Three” arrived. At that time, Ponyville was in the middle of an agricultural reform, and the security forces of Ponyville were organizing to cut down the apple trees in Sweet Apple Acres. On the one hand, the cut wood would be used as fuel reserves, and on the other hand, more cold-resistant crops would be planted. Starlight Glimmer escaped to Sweet Apple Acres, took advantage of the chaos to steal some wood as a poor substitute for the train fuel, and hijacked a train that stopped in Ponyville, fleeing Ponyville with other fugitives. Although the train encountered an “accident” that was suspected to be planned by Cozy Glow on the way, Starlight was still lucky enough to survive, and arrived in Our Town in the autumn of 1000.\n\nOur Town is a remote small village. Even if the M6 had visited here, it did not attract the attention of Canterlot. In fact, if you ask a pony from Canterlot about Our Town, the most common response should be “What?”. Thanks to the obscurity of Our Town, Starlight was able to settle down and evade the pursuit of the Empire. Due to the lack of information, in this remote corner of the northeast of the central continent of Equestria, Our Town had not even received the news of the Ultimate Battle. When Starlight told them that Canterlot had fallen, the residents of the town were also frightened and quickly united. The residents followed Starlight Glimmer and her companions, and quickly assembled a crude but determined uprising army.\n\nIn the winter of 1001, she finally got in contact with Discord, who had escaped from the Ultimate Battle with her. He was now hiding in the Everfree Forest and fighting a guerrilla war against the Empire. Although Discord had lost his magic, the existence of an ally who could cooperate with Starlight was still good news. Starlight and Discord quickly established the United Resistance, intending to attack the Empire when Cozy Glow was not yet stable in power. But it was already too late. The winter of 1001 is already two years after the Ultimate Battle, and Cozy Glow has gradually stabilized the situation, and the counterattack was swift. The United Resistance was able to advance for a small distance towards the Empire, but soon began to retreat. Before the front line of Starlight and Discord was cut off by the Empire, Discord gave Starlight a precious item that was found in the ruins of Twilight’s Castle — a diary. Starlight knew that it was the diary that connected the two worlds. When Starlight finally contacted the human world through the diary, her tears soaked the paper, which made Sunset Shimmer, who was looking at the blurred words on the diary, feel puzzled.\n\nTime passed quickly, and Starlight was busy with organization and construction work everywhere. She felt excited when she heard about the distant victory of the zebras on the Changelinia continent, and felt painful when she remembered that her former best friend, Trixie, had been serving Cozy Glow for two years. Now Starlight Glimmer only had Sunburst as a good friend by her side, but no matter what, Starlight believed in hope. The Empire built by the “Big Three”, which seemed unshakable, was little more than sand castles, only the tides of liberation, were forever.\n\nIt is now the winter of 1002. The resistance army is still alive, inheriting the will of Celestia and Twilight, preserving the fire of harmonism. It has become a haven, a beacon of Equestria, illuminating the hope of all ponies.

